# Third-party corpora. The bulk payloads stay local — upstream owns them, and a
# clone pinned to a commit is more recoverable than a copy vendored into our
# history. research/README.md IS tracked and names every expected clone with its
# URL and pinned commit, so losing one is never silent.
#
# This repo is why the rule exists: on 2026-08-10 macula-greek and
# morphgnt-sblgnt were both found missing with no deletion trace, because a
# blanket `research/` ignore leaves nothing behind to notice an absence. Fifteen
# validators had been returning zero, and M4-GNT-1 had been emitting 4158
# candidates against a baseline of 409. Nothing failed loudly.
#
# Our own analysis does NOT belong here. It goes in the numbered tiers —
# evidence in 2-evidence/, scripts in 5-machinery/ — where git can recover it.
research/*
!research/README.md

# Private strategy docs (not on public repo)
# Pattern mirrors readers-lxx: ignore all of private/ except the README stub
/private/*
!/private/README.md

# Machine-specific Claude Code permissions (cross-project paths that shouldn't be public)
# Both files are machine-specific; the harness auto-writes permissions to settings.json.
# Gitignoring both prevents GitHub Desktop churn every time a new path is approved.
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Regenerable v4 generation draft (not the v4-editorial source-of-truth)
data/text-files/v4-sblgnt-draft/

# R9-binding experiment scratch (regenerable; promoted to v1.5/grk only on deploy)
data/text-files/v1.5-binding-experiment/
